Insane what you can create with three.js nowadays.

I made a game-quality 3D experience in the browser with water ripples, smoke effects, a 3D paper menu, underwater UI, and a peeling footer.

The whole thing is pure code and only 183 KB. Seriously, no loading screen needed.

I combined http://canvasui.dev and http://threeui.com components with a few direct prompts:

- Open the hamburger menu as a 3D paper overlay {threeui 3D paper}
- Add a peel effect to the footer {canvasui peel}
- When the cursor passes through the heading, turn the letters into smoke {canvasui liquid object}

Inspired by the amazing http://unseen.co site.

Let me know if I should open-source it.

